  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "type": "overview",
      "label": "Start",
      "title": "Three ways to build a participle",
      "learn": [
        "Weak verbs take ge- and -t: gefragt. A stem in -t or -d takes -et: gewartet. öffnen does too: geöffnet.",
        "A separable prefix keeps ge- in the middle: eingekauft, angerufen. be-, er-, ver- and -ieren take no ge-: bezahlt, erklärt, untersucht, dokumentiert.",
        "Strong verbs take ge- and -en: gesehen. The vowel often changes: geschrieben, genommen. messen → gemessen, not gemesst."
      ],
      "minutes": 25,
      "vocab": [
        { "de": "Befund", "article": "der", "plural": "die Befunde", "en": "finding, report", "emoji": "📄", "glossaryKey": "befund" },
        { "de": "Patient", "article": "der", "plural": "die Patienten", "en": "patient (male)", "emoji": "🧑🏽", "glossaryKey": "patient" },
        { "de": "Tablette", "article": "die", "plural": "die Tabletten", "en": "tablet", "emoji": "💊", "glossaryKey": "tablette" },
        { "de": "Akte", "article": "die", "plural": "die Akten", "en": "chart", "emoji": "📋", "glossaryKey": "akte" },
        { "de": "Fieber", "article": "das", "en": "fever", "emoji": "🌡️", "glossaryKey": "fieber" },
        { "de": "Zimmer", "article": "das", "plural": "die Zimmer", "en": "room", "emoji": "🛏️", "glossaryKey": "zimmer" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Wie heißt das Partizip?",
        "de": "Der Arzt hat den Befund gesehen. Die Tochter hat eingekauft. Der Patient hat bezahlt. Ich habe gewartet. Der Arzt hat den Patienten untersucht. Die Pflegekraft hat den Befund geschrieben.",
        "en": "The doctor has seen the report. The daughter has done the shopping. The patient has paid. I waited. The doctor has examined the patient. The nurse has written the report."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "ge-, no ge-, or a new vowel",
      "practice": "choose",
      "heroTitle": "gesehen, eingekauft, bezahlt",
      "heroImage": "clipboard",
      "story": [
        "Chapters 24 and 25 chose <b>haben</b> or <b>sein</b>. The participle still closes the sentence. This chapter builds that participle.",
        "Weak: <b>ge-</b> plus the stem plus <b>-t</b>. fragen → <b>gefragt</b>. machen → <b>gemacht</b>. A stem in <b>-t</b> or <b>-d</b> takes <b>-et</b>: warten → <b>gewartet</b>, arbeiten → <b>gearbeitet</b>. öffnen → <b>geöffnet</b>.",
        "Separable: the prefix stays, and <b>ge-</b> sits in the middle. einkaufen → <b>eingekauft</b>. abholen → <b>abgeholt</b>. anrufen → <b>angerufen</b>.",
        "No <b>ge-</b> after <b>be-, er-, ver-</b>, or on an <b>-ieren</b> verb. bezahlen → <b>bezahlt</b>. erklären → <b>erklärt</b>. untersuchen → <b>untersucht</b>. dokumentieren → <b>dokumentiert</b>. bekommen stays <b>bekommen</b>.",
        "Strong: <b>ge-</b> plus <b>-en</b>, often with a new vowel. sehen → <b>gesehen</b>. schreiben → <b>geschrieben</b>. trinken → <b>getrunken</b>. nehmen → <b>genommen</b>. messen → <b>gemessen</b>, not gemesst."
      ],
      "questionRule": "Weak: ge- + t, or -et after -t/-d. Separable: prefix + ge-. No ge- after be-/er-/ver- or on -ieren. Strong: ge- + en.",
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Schwach: ge- + t",
          "caption": "Stem in -t or -d, and öffnen: add -et.",
          "columns": ["Infinitiv", "Partizip"],
          "rows": [
            { "label": "fragen", "cells": ["fragen", "gefragt"], "highlight": true },
            { "label": "machen", "cells": ["machen", "gemacht"] },
            { "label": "warten", "cells": ["warten", "gewartet"], "highlight": true },
            { "label": "öffnen", "cells": ["öffnen", "geöffnet"] },
            { "label": "arbeiten", "cells": ["arbeiten", "gearbeitet"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Trennbar, oder ohne ge-",
          "caption": "Separable: prefix + ge- in the middle. be-, er-, ver- and -ieren: no ge-.",
          "columns": ["Infinitiv", "Partizip"],
          "rows": [
            { "label": "einkaufen", "cells": ["einkaufen", "eingekauft"], "highlight": true },
            { "label": "abholen", "cells": ["abholen", "abgeholt"] },
            { "label": "anrufen", "cells": ["anrufen", "angerufen"] },
            { "label": "bezahlen", "cells": ["bezahlen", "bezahlt"], "highlight": true },
            { "label": "erklären", "cells": ["erklären", "erklärt"] },
            { "label": "untersuchen", "cells": ["untersuchen", "untersucht"] },
            { "label": "dokumentieren", "cells": ["dokumentieren", "dokumentiert"] },
            { "label": "bekommen", "cells": ["bekommen", "bekommen"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Stark: ge- + en",
          "caption": "The vowel often changes. verstehen → verstanden: ver- blocks ge-.",
          "columns": ["Infinitiv", "Partizip"],
          "rows": [
            { "label": "sehen", "cells": ["sehen", "gesehen"], "highlight": true },
            { "label": "schreiben", "cells": ["schreiben", "geschrieben"] },
            { "label": "trinken", "cells": ["trinken", "getrunken"] },
            { "label": "nehmen", "cells": ["nehmen", "genommen"] },
            { "label": "sprechen", "cells": ["sprechen", "gesprochen"] },
            { "label": "essen", "cells": ["essen", "gegessen"] },
            { "label": "messen", "cells": ["messen", "gemessen"], "highlight": true },
            { "label": "helfen", "cells": ["helfen", "geholfen"] }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "warning": {
        "title": "Three familiar wrong builds",
        "items": [
          { "de": "Der Arzt hat den Befund gesehen.", "en": "Strong: gesehen, not geseht.", "tone": "ok" },
          { "de": "Der Arzt hat den Befund geseht.", "en": "sehen does not take -t.", "tone": "stop" },
          { "de": "Die Tochter hat eingekauft.", "en": "The prefix stays on the participle.", "tone": "ok" },
          { "de": "Die Tochter hat gekauft ein.", "en": "ein does not split off in the participle.", "tone": "stop" },
          { "de": "Der Arzt hat den Patienten untersucht.", "en": "untersuchen takes no ge-.", "tone": "ok" },
          { "de": "Der Arzt hat den Patienten geuntersucht.", "en": "ge- does not go in front of unter-.", "tone": "stop" }
        ],
        "tip": "Ask three questions: Is there a separable prefix? Is the start be-, er-, ver-, or -ieren? Is the verb strong? Otherwise ge- plus -t."
      },
